course: dictionary
lesson: 13719
title: Instructional
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some texts exist to teach you how to do something. The word instructional describes them: it means meant to teach or show you how to do something. «The instructional video showed us how to tie a knot.» The video did not just entertain us. It taught us a skill.
explain: Instructional writing, like recipes and how-to guides, uses numbered steps and bossy verbs such as cut, mix and fold. «Step 1: Cut the apple into thin slices. Step 2: Fold the paper in half.» When you see steps and commands like these, you are probably reading instructional writing.
explain: In formal language, instructional can also mean to do with teaching in schools. «Instructional time starts at nine o'clock.» Here it means lesson time, not a skill to copy at home. The words around it show you which meaning fits.
fact: Instructional means meant to teach or show you how to do something.
fact: Instructional texts often use numbered steps and bossy verbs like cut, mix and fold.
fact: «Instructional video» and «instructional text» are common phrases for something that teaches a skill.
fact: «Instructional time» is a formal phrase meaning time for teaching and lessons in school.
exercise: «The instructional video showed us how to tie a knot.» What does instructional mean here? | *Meant to teach you how to do something | Made of wood | Loud and noisy | Very funny and silly
exercise: Which text is instructional writing? | A letter to a friend about the weekend | A poem about the sea | *A recipe with numbered steps: 1. Mix the flour. 2. Fold in the eggs | A story about a dragon
exercise: «Instructional time ends at three o'clock.» In this sentence, instructional is to do with what? | *Teaching and lessons in school | Sports and games at home | Cooking and food | Weather and the sky
test: «The instructional book had a clear picture for every step.» What is the book for? | Listing the names of birds | *Teaching you how to do a task step by step | Keeping a secret diary | Telling a scary ghost story
test: Which bossy verb is often found in instructional writing? | *Cut | Wonder | Sleep | Dream
exam: Which sentence uses instructional with the school meaning? | «We had an instructional picnic by the lake.» | «The instructional dog ran across the park.» | *«Instructional time starts at nine o'clock.» | «The instructional video was very long.»
